slml 0.2
use"layout.slml"

doc{$title"Command line"
  t.lead"`slml` opens original documents in its own native browser. Run `slml --help` or `man slml` for a summary."
  section{$id"compile" $title"Opening documents"
    c{g0
      ref{$name"slml page.slml" $values"native browser" $about"Read the original SLML document and draw it directly."}
      ref{$name"slml site/" $values"site/index.slml" $about"Open the site's home page. The folder is the root for absolute paths."}
      ref{$name"slml handbook/" $values"native handbook" $about"Read this guide in SLML's own browser."}
    }
  }
  section{$id"export" $title"Explicit exports"
    c{g0
      ref{$name"slml build page.slml" $values"page.html" $about"Optional HTML compatibility export."}
      ref{$name"slml build site/ -o public/" $values"HTML folder" $about"Export a site for an existing HTML web host."}
      ref{$name"slml page.slml -o out.html" $values"HTML file" $about"An explicit output path also selects export mode."}
      ref{$name"slml render page.slml -o page.png" $values"native PNG" $about"Save a picture with SLML's renderer."}
    }
  }
  section{$id"commands" $title"Commands"
    c{g0
      ref{$name"slml check …" $values"files or folders" $about"Report errors without writing anything. Exit status 1 on errors."}
      ref{$name"slml serve [folder]" $values"--port, --open, --web, --html" $about"Serve original SLML sources. --open launches the native browser; --web or --html explicitly selects a web-browser adapter."}
      ref{$name"slml view page-or-folder" $values"--scale" $about"Explicit form of the default native browser action."}
      ref{$name"slml render page.slml" $values"-o, --width, --scale" $about"Render to PNG (same as -o page.png)."}
      ref{$name"slml upgrade …" $values"files or folders, --check" $about"Rewrite slml 0.1 files in the short slml 0.2 syntax and re-format 0.2 files. Nothing is written unless every page stays exactly the same. --check only lists files that would change."}
    }
  }
  section{$id"upgrade" $title"Upgrading older files"
    "Pages written in the long syntax of SLML 0.1 still open, but the current syntax is 0.2. Convert a whole site at once:"
    code"""
        slml upgrade my-site/          # rewrite every .slml file in place
        slml upgrade --check my-site/  # only list files that would change
        """
    "Before writing, `slml upgrade` compiles every page from the old and the new files, imports included, and refuses to write anything if a single page would differ. Comments are kept. Running it on 0.2 files gives them the standard formatting, so it also works as a formatter."
  }
  section{$id"options" $title"Options"
    c{g0
      ref{$name"-o, --output" $values"path" $about"Explicitly export a file or folder; .png uses the native image renderer, other output paths select HTML."}
      ref{$name"--root" $values"folder" $about"What paths starting with / refer to. Default: the current folder if the file is inside it, otherwise the file's folder. When building a folder, that folder."}
      ref{$name"--width" $values"pixels" $about"Page width for PNG output (default 900)."}
      ref{$name"--scale" $values"number" $about"Pixel density for PNG and the viewer, e.g. 2 for sharp screens."}
      ref{$name"--port" $values"number" $about"First port serve tries (default 4000)."}
      ref{$name"--open" $values"" $about"serve: open the native SLML browser. With --web or --html, open the explicitly selected web adapter."}
      ref{$name"--web" $values"" $about"serve: opt into the optional WebAssembly viewer hosted in a web browser."}
      ref{$name"--html" $values"" $about"Explicit HTML export or HTML server preview."}
      ref{$name"-q, --quiet" $values"" $about"Print only errors."}
      ref{$name"-V, --version" $values"" $about"Compiler and language version."}
    }
  }
  section{$id"viewer" $title"The native browser"
    "`slml` shows a page with SLML's own renderer in its own native window. The page reloads when you save it, its imports or its images. External links open in your normal web browser; hovering a link shows where it goes at the bottom of the window."
    c{g0
      ref{$name"wheel, ↑ ↓, PgUp PgDn" $values"scroll" $about"Also Space and Shift+Space, Home and End. Drag the scrollbar or click its track."}
      ref{$name"click, Enter" $values"follow a link" $about"Links darken under the pointer and while pressed."}
      ref{$name"Tab, Shift+Tab" $values"move focus" $about"Through links and form fields in reading order, with a visible ring."}
      ref{$name"Alt+← →, Backspace" $values"history" $about"Back and forward; the mouse's side buttons work too. The scroll position is restored."}
      ref{$name"F5, Ctrl+R" $values"reload" $about"Reload by hand."}
      ref{$name"Ctrl + − 0, Ctrl+wheel" $values"zoom" $about"Zoom in, out and back to 100%."}
      ref{$name"drag, double, triple click" $values"select text" $about"Shift+click extends, Ctrl+A selects all, Ctrl+C copies (needs wl-clipboard or xclip on Linux)."}
      ref{$name"Ctrl+F" $values"find" $about"Highlights every match; Enter or F3 goes to the next, Shift for the previous, Esc closes."}
      ref{$name"F12, Ctrl+Shift+I" $values"inspect" $about"Point at an element to see its box, padding, attributes and the file and line it was written on; click pins it."}
      ref{$name"Ctrl+W" $values"close" $about"Close the window."}
    }
    "Forms work too: type into fields, tick boxes, pick options and send. See [Forms](/forms.slml#sending)."
  }
  section{$id"exit" $title"Exit status"
    "`0` on success; `1` if checking, export or opening a window fails. In the interactive browser an invalid page appears as an SLML error page. Use `slml check` for automated validation."
  }
  pager{$prev"/website-tutorial.slml" $prev-label"A complete website" $next"/errors.slml" $next-label"Understanding errors"}
}
